messages:
priya.k: Quick sync — we need to pick a single guidance for fetch in the JS SDK v2 (ESM + CJS + Edge). FWIW customers keep hitting confusing errors in Next.js Edge and Node 16 apps.
alex.w: Agree. My vote: prefer global fetch when available, fallback to undici for Node <18. Keep the fallback lazy-imported.
sam: How do we communicate that without confusing types/bundlers? people hit rollup/webpack issues if they import undici at bundle time.
priya.k: Exactly — guidance should show a runtime guard + snippet. Also call out package.json exports and dual cjs/esm builds so bundlers don't pull undici into edge builds.
olivia: Example snippet we used in an internal sample:
```
// runtime-safe fetch chooser
let _fetch;
if (typeof fetch === 'function') {
  _fetch = fetch;
} else {
  // lazy import so bundlers don't include undici in edge builds
  const { fetch: undiciFetch } = await import('undici');
  _fetch = undiciFetch;
}
const res = await _fetch(url, opts);
```
sam: Nice. For types we should export a typed wrapper so SDK consumers get correct signatures regardless of runtime. e.g. `export type Fetch = typeof fetch;` and `export function setFetch(f: Fetch) { ... }`.
priya.k: UX note: default behavior should "just work" for Node >=18 and browser/edge. For older node, we ship a dev-dependency suggestion: `npm i undici` and fallback runtime import. Add a one-liner in README and a troubleshooting section for common errors.
alex.w: Also call out Next.js/Edge: recommend using platform fetch only; if user bundles SDK for edge, ensure bundler tree-shakes undici. Add a short e2e sample in our next.js example app to show correct pattern.
devx-bot: Related doc: <https://internal.redwood.dev/sdk/fetch-guidance> (updated 2026-02-03) :white_check_mark:
priya.k: I'll draft the README blurb + code sample and a tiny test that asserts SDK does not import undici in edge bundle. Tagging @olivia for sample app PR.
olivia: On it — will open PR after the README draft.
priya.k: Thanks — if no objections I'll lock this as our guidance and add to the migration checklist.
